  "_comment": "Daily and weekly operational tasks (DESIGN.md §11, Operations), read by Operations and checked by Operations.problems() when the items load. reset: when the sets change, in UTC: every day at daily_hour_utc, every week on weekly_day (0 Monday ... 6 Sunday) at weekly_hour_utc. kinds: per set, how many tasks it rolls (count), its reward_scale (times a band's money and XP), the chance a finished task also gives a rare item (rare_chance), the Drip each task pays (drip, per task; DESIGN.md §6.7) and how many re-rolls each task has (rerolls). bands: the player-level bands (from: the band's first level) with a daily task's base roubles and xp in that band. A task pays base × kind reward_scale × its template's reward (for the band) × its count ÷ the middle of the band's count range, roubles rounded to 500 and XP to 50. reroll_fee: a re-roll costs this share of the task's roubles. all_dailies_bonus: claiming all of a day's dailies pays this share of the band's daily roubles and XP on top. rare_items: what a rare item roll can give, never found in raid: each entry's item, count and weight, from player level `level` (at the roll); every item Rare or better (min_rarity), Epic or rarer only from epic_level. templates: {id, name, kind (daily / weekly), levels [first, last] (player levels it can be rolled at), weight (how often it's picked, 1 when left out), objective (a quest objective, DESIGN.md §11, without its count; faction \"rival\" means the other faction's PMCs), pick (lists the roll picks one from: map, item, weapon_class, station; poi_tiers: a point of interest of these tiers on the picked map), counts ([low, high] per band; none for visit), reward (one weight, or one per band)}. Only playable maps, stations you've built that have crafts and weapon classes you have or can buy are picked; a template with nothing left to pick isn't rolled.",
